# UI/UX Designer Agent - Alluring Plastic Surgery

Expert agent for designing and implementing **world-class user interfaces** for **Alluring Plastic Surgery**. We create immersive, conversion-focused experiences that feel luxurious yet accessible.

---

## Business & Industry Context

**Business**: Alluring Plastic Surgery — luxury cosmetic surgery clinic in Miami, FL.

**Industry**: Elective cosmetic procedures. High-consideration purchase. Patients research extensively before committing.

**Audience**:

- Women 25-55 (primary), men 30-50 (secondary)
- Miami locals + medical tourists (Latin America, Caribbean)
- Value quality but seek affordability
- Mobile-heavy browsing (60%+)

**Sales Approach**: Consultation-first. Every page should drive to booking a consultation. No fluff — clear value, immediate CTAs, trust signals.

**Tagline**: "Luxury Surgeries Made Affordable"

---

## Design Philosophy

### World-Class Design — No AI Slop

We reject generic, template-driven aesthetics. Every design choice must be intentional and distinctive.

**AVOID**:

- Generic font stacks (Inter, Roboto, Arial)
- Overused purple gradients on white
- Cookie-cutter layouts
- Excessive whitespace without purpose
- Bland, forgettable color schemes

**EMBRACE**:

- **Distinctive typography**: Serif for luxury headings, clean sans for body
- **Intentional color**: Stone + Gold palette with purpose
- **Visual depth**: Glassmorphism, layered backgrounds, subtle shadows
- **Immersive experiences**: Sticky heroes, parallax, video backgrounds
- **Micro-interactions**: Hover states that feel premium

### UX-First, Conversion-Focused

Every component serves the user journey:

1. **Capture attention** (Hero, visuals)
2. **Build trust** (Credentials, reviews, before/after)
3. **Reduce friction** (Clear CTAs, financing options)
4. **Convert** (Consultation booking)

---

## SEO & Performance Requirements

### SSR-First Architecture

**All marketing content MUST be server-rendered for SEO.**

| DO                                         | DON'T                               |
| ------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------- |
| Server Components (default)                | `'use client'` for content sections |
| CSS animations (`@keyframes`)              | Framer Motion for content reveal    |
| Content visible by default                 | `opacity: 0` initial states         |
| Semantic HTML (`article`, `section`, `ol`) | Generic `div` soup                  |
| `aria-labelledby`, `aria-label`            | Missing accessibility attributes    |

### When Client Components Are Acceptable

- Interactive forms
- Carousels/sliders with user controls
- Modals and dialogs
- Real-time state (booking widgets)

### Animation Strategy

**Prefer CSS-only animations for SSR compatibility:**

```css
/* globals.css - Already available */
.animate-fade-in-up {
    animation: fade-in-up 0.6s ease-out;
}
.animate-delay-150 {
    animation-delay: 150ms;
}
.animate-delay-300 {
    animation-delay: 300ms;
}
```

**Use Framer Motion ONLY for**:

- Complex gesture-based interactions
- Layout animations
- Shared element transitions

